      "date": "2026-04-17T16:19:00.000Z",
      "title": "Crisil Limited Approves Final Dividend for the Year Ended December 31, 2025",
      "body": "CRISIL Limited at its AGM to be held on April 17, 2026 approved final dividend on equity shares of INR 28 per equity share of face value of Re.1/- and to approve and confirm the declaration and payment of three interim dividends aggregating INR 33 per equity share for the year ended December 31, 2025.",
      "keyDevTypeId": "46",
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "EventActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "ec883518-8d7e-4934-9203-e5d436517114",
      "type": "narrative-update",
      "date": "2026-04-15T00:21:15.000Z",
      "title": "CRISIL: Future Dividend Payout Will Support A Constructive Share Price Outlook",
      "body": "Analysts have lowered their price target on CRISIL from ₹5,106.50 to ₹4,632.00, reflecting updated assumptions on the discount rate, revenue growth, profit margins, and future P/E expectations. What's in the News CRISIL Limited has recommended a final dividend of ₹28 per equity share of face value ₹1 for the financial year ended December 31, 2025, subject to shareholder approval at the Annual General Meeting scheduled for April 17, 2026 (company disclosure).",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": "https://simplywall.st/community/narratives/in/diversified-financials/nse-crisil/crisil-shares/lvpkc24n-crisil-stable-financials-and-interim-dividend-will-support-balanced-outlook/updates/12-analysts-have-lowered-their-price-target-on-crisil-from-indian-rupee51",
      "raw_subtype": "narrative-update"
    },
    {
      "id": "8c529f70-72d6-4154-8506-72f3529e8169",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-04-14T18:55:10.000Z",
      "title": "Price target decreased by 9.3% to ₹4,632",
      "body": "Down from ₹5,107, the current price target is an average from 2 analysts. New target price is 14% above last closing price of ₹4,055. Stock is down 7.0% over the past year. The company is forecast to post earnings per share of ₹111 for next year compared to ₹105 last year.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "40e2e840-7d07-41e0-9fd4-54aedbb2e614",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-03-28T19:27:53.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2025 earnings: Revenues exceed analysts expectations while EPS lags behind",
      "body": "Full year 2025 results: EPS: ₹105 (up from ₹93.55 in FY 2024). Revenue: ₹36.5b (up 12% from FY 2024). Net income: ₹7.66b (up 12% from FY 2024). Profit margin: 21% (in line with FY 2024). Revenue exceeded analyst estimates by 1.8%. Earnings per share (EPS) missed analyst estimates by 2.1%. Revenue is forecast to grow 12% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 17% growth forecast for the Capital Markets industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 10% per year whereas the company’s share price has increased by 6% per year.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "e624bf48-bc99-4a15-b9ab-5f7ca6ba502a",
      "type": "brief",
